From ce130f9221143c4d085e8f688a5a430d638310ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohannSSK <321048248+JohannSSK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:02:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Cut prompt latency and split the backend into one module
 per concern
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Latency. Each check ran as its own `python scanner.py` subprocess, so every
prompt paid three interpreter start-ups and re-imported torch and spaCy
from scratch. Worse, context.py and injection.py each built the *same*
zero-shot model, so it loaded twice.

- New src/MLscripts/model_cache.py: one lazy, shared cache. spaCy is
  loaded on first use instead of at import, and the zero-shot classifier is
  built once and shared by both checks that need it.
- The three scanners now expose analyze(text). analyze_stdin() and the
  __main__ block are unchanged, so tools/evaluate.py still drives them as
  scripts.
- New src/scanners.py runs each check in-process; the subprocess protocol
  stays as a fallback, so a missing model degrades instead of breaking.
- Models are warmed on a background thread at start-up, so nobody's first
  message waits for torch.

Structure. app.py was 950 lines holding every route, helper and query.

- config, db, errors, web, passwords, members, ai_client, scanning,
  block_log, chat_store each own one job; routes/ holds one blueprint per
  area (pages, admin_api, member_api, chat_api, chat_history).
- app.py is now a create_app() factory that wires them together.
- admin_session no longer re-implements token hashing: it shares auth's.
- http.py renamed to web.py — it was shadowing the standard library.

Features the new pages need.

- Messages carry an id and a timestamp, which is what makes editing,
  deleting and regenerating a single message possible.
- New chat search across a member's own messages.
- New ACTIVITY_LOG records every step (sign-in, send, block, override,
  policy change) with a timestamp, and team_stats now returns per-member
  trends and a merged timeline for the statistics page.
- An approved override is recorded but never counted as a block.

All 21 authorisation tests still pass.

