From 391e248637bd1fbcd438a123b13a2a0945c35a48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:09:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Rebuild the frontend as split, single-purpose modules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The UI had grown into three files that everything lived in: style.css
(1582 lines), main.js (1510 lines) and index.html. Each is now a set of
modules that does one job, and the last of the three is gone.

Structure
- css: base (tokens, reset), components (buttons, fields, toasts, modal,
  scan overlay), auth (the login portal, untouched visually), workspace
  (chat), page (the shell shared by the signed-in pages), stats (charts).
- js/core: dom, icons, api, loading, markdown, shell — no page logic.
- js: auth, workspace, profile, settings, stats, team — one per page.
- templates: base.html plus partials/sidebar.html, so the navigation is
  defined once instead of copied into five pages.

Pages that were overlays or missing are now real routes: /profile,
/settings, /stats, /team, /help. /stats charts per-member activity with a
timestamped timeline, drawn with divs and CSS so nothing loads from a CDN.

Icons
27 PNGs under assets/icons. The designs live in one place — the SVG table
in core/icons.js, which the browser inlines as vectors — and
tools/build_icons.py parses that same table and rasterises every entry, so
the two can never drift apart. tools/icons/ is a small Pillow-only SVG
rasteriser (path, circle, rect, ellipse, line, polyline, polygon) written
because no Cairo backend is available here.

Fixes
- In-chat search filtered by hiding nodes and then re-rendered, which threw
  the filter away. Rendering now applies the query itself, and
  Dom.highlightText walks text nodes so highlighting cannot break rendered
  markdown or inject markup.
- assets/ is served at /assets/<path>, which was 404ing every icon.
- Sidebar icons are PNGs, so they cannot follow currentColor; resting and
  active states are separated by opacity instead.

tools/smoke.py drives the whole app over HTTP: 22 checks covering sign-in,
member management, settings, chat search, authorisation refusals and every
page route.

